Explain the difference between “systemctl start”, “systemctl enable”, and “systemctl
status”. When would you use each?

Start starts now, not on boot and changes the runtime state. Used to start a service immediately.
Enable starts at boot, changes boot config. Used when you want a service to persist across reboots etc.
status shows current process status, doesn't change anything. Usesd to check if a srvice is running.


